  "order": 11,
  "blocks": [
    {
      "id": "bzet1n3",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "1. Definition of Adjective"
    },
    {
      "type": "keyFacts",
      "title": "Key Takeaways",
      "items": [
        "Adjectives modify, qualify, or add meaning to nouns and pronouns.",
        "Types include Quality, Quantity, Number, Demonstrative, Possessive, Interrogative, and Distributive adjectives.",
        "Adjectives of Quantity answer 'how much' (uncountable nouns), while Adjectives of Number answer 'how many' (countable nouns).",
        "Degrees of comparison include Positive (base quality), Comparative (comparing two), and Superlative (comparing three or more).",
        "Formation of comparative and superlative forms typically uses suffixes (-er/-est) or prefixes (more/most), with special rules for irregular forms."
      ],
      "id": "ltwjp07"
    },
