    {
      "type": "examAlert",
      "items": [
        "Avoid double comparatives and superlatives (e.g., 'more wiser' or 'most smartest' are incorrect).",
        "Differentiate strictly between 'fewer' (used with countable nouns/Adjective of Number) and 'less' (used with uncountable nouns/Adjective of Quantity).",
        "When comparing two things, always use the Comparative degree, even if the group consists of only two items.",
        "Certain adjectives like 'unique', 'perfect', 'complete', and 'supreme' express absolute qualities and cannot take comparative or superlative forms."
      ],
      "id": "v56dghq"
